DisplayPort audio over USB-C - WORK IN PROGRESS, NOT IN THE SERIES
(2026-09-24, docs/phase4-usb-dp-scoping.md "DP audio")

Applies on top of kernel/patches/00*. What it does:
- DTS: MultiMedia3 front end (PCM 2), a "DisplayPort Playback" back end
  (q6afedai DISPLAY_PORT_RX -> q6routing -> &mdss_dp); the DP0 jack
  follows the monitor.
- q6afe-dai: start the DP AFE port from trigger instead of prepare (the
  msm DP codec enables its audio engine in its own prepare, after ours).
- q6afe: send AFE_PARAM_ID_HDMI_DP_MST_VID_IDX_CFG / _DPTX_IDX_CFG (0/0)
  before the config, like downstream afe_set_display_stream().
- msm dp_audio: prepare with no monitor powered returns 0 instead of
  -EINVAL (PipeWire probes every PCM of the verb; one failing open drops
  the whole profile - the speakers vanished), plus a debug print.
- UCM: SectionDevice "HDMI1" on hw:X,2, JackControl "DP0 Jack",
  priority 50, route in the verb.

Status: the DSP accepts the stream/ctl index and the HDMI config params
but never answers AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START for port 0x6020 (-110), with
a monitor up and msm_dp_audio_prepare run (2 channels). Without a
monitor the start always times out. Next: capture stock (DeX with audio)
in the stock-boot pass.

